    "https://careers.westernsydney.edu.au/job/manager-industry-innovation-in-bankstown-au-jid-583": {
      "title": "Manager, Industry Innovation",
      "description": "Manager, Industry Innovation Division Research and Innovation (U79) __jobinformationwidget.freetext.LocationText__ Bankstown, AU Contract Type Full-Time Job ID: REF1915W Apply Shortlist Full-time, Fixed-Term position at HEW Level 9 until December 2027. Bankstown City Campus Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead industry partnerships and the Factory of the Future to translate university capability into practical regional outcomes. The Opportunity You will contribute to the Industry Innovation portfolio, by connecting University expertise, facilities, research and technology with the needs of industry and the Western Sydney region. You will develop partnerships that support research collaboration, workforce development, student engagement and applied industry projects. You will oversee the operational management of the Factory of the Future as an advanced manufacturing innovation facility. This includes enabling technology demonstrations, training and collaboration for students, researchers and industry, while maintaining effective planning, governance, risk management and reporting. You will also identify commercial partnerships and government funding opportunities that strengthen the portfolio’s sustainability and impact. Through work-integrated learning, skills training and applied innovation experiences, you will create pathways for students to engage with industry and contribute to practical outcomes. What Success Looks Like: Operate the Factory of the Future as an effective platform for collaboration, technology demonstration and training. Build strategic partnerships that generate research, workforce development, student engagement and industry opportunities. Translate University research, expertise, facilities and technology into practical solutions for industry and the community. Progress commercial partnership and government funding opportunities that strengthen portfolio sustainability. Deliver effective governance, planning, risk management, reporting and continuous improvement across the portfolio. Please refer to the Position Description for full details. About You A relevant postgraduate qualification in engineering, project management or a related field, or an equivalent combination of technical, higher education and management experience. Demonstrated experience leading complex programs, facilities or portfolios involving multiple stakeholders and measurable outcomes. Proven ability to develop strategic partnerships with industry, government, research organisations and other external stakeholders. Experience translating innovation, research collaboration, industry engagement or commercial initiatives into practical outcomes. Strong financial, governance and operational management skills, supported by effective communication, negotiation and stakeholder influence. Benefits We invest in the people who make our mission possible. Alongside a rewarding career, we offer a range of benefits designed to support your financial, personal and family wellbeing. Financial benefits: Access to staff-only products and offers with selected banking partners, salary sacrifice options for onsite parking, and novated motor vehicle leasing. Health and wellbeing support: Free Employee Assistance Program (EAP), complimentary annual flu vaccination, eligibility for Fitness Passport membership, and access to discounted private health cover. Onsite childcare: Long day care and early learning services operate at our Campbelltown, Hawkesbury, Parramatta, and Penrith campuses. Staff may be eligible for discounted fees and salary packaging, with places subject to centre capacity. Application Details Position Enquiries: Direct to Anna Lin, Senior Manager, Partnerships and Precinct Activation via Anna.Lin@westernsydney.edu.au . Please include the job reference code REF1915W. Closing Date: 11:59pm, Wednesday 28 October 2026. Checks: Appointment to this position is subject to a valid Working with Children Check (WWCC) for paid employment in accordance with the Child Protection (Working with Children) Act 2012 (NSW). Working Rights: You must provide evidence of full-time working rights in Australia at application. How to Apply: Please note that only applications submitted via the University’s online recruitment system will be considered. As part of your online application, you will be asked to respond to screening questions addressing the key qualifications, experiences and skills required for this position. Belonging at Western We are committed to substantive equality as outlined in our Equal Opportunity Policy . We actively encourage applications from Indigenous Australians, candidates of all gender identities and expressions, people of all abilities, and those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. For Reasonable Adjustments during the application process, please contact talentacquisitionteam@westernsydney.edu.au . About Western This is your opportunity to be part of something bigger. By joining Western Sydney University, you become a valued member of our community. As our region changes, so too does our university. Western is boldly different, energetic, global, diverse, dynamic, and youthful. Our mission is to deliver student success, impactful research, and stronger communities. As part of our team, you will have a stake in shaping the future of education, broadening horizons, and changing lives. Making a difference starts at Western. For the latest please visit our website and LinkedIn . Apply Shortlist Share ABOUT WESTERN Western Sydney University was established in 1989, bringing together a number of existing higher education institutions across the region to create a single, unified university for Western Sydney. Founded with a strong commitment to accessibility and community engagement, the University was designed to expand educational opportunities for one of Australia’s most diverse and rapidly growing regions. Over the years, it has evolved into a world-class institution known for its innovation, research excellence, and focus on equity and social justice—continuing to play a vital role in shaping the future of Greater Western Sydney and beyond. List #1 Some roles you might be interested in Lecturer (Chemistry) Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Engineering, Computing & Science (U73K) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Ongoing position at Academic Level B.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements. Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Teach chemistry, d Reference 4ee3304b-a192-44f8-be8d-507908406a1f Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Lecturer in Finance Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Faculty of Soc.Sciences,Art,Business,Education&Law (U73L) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Academic Description Full-time, Fixed-Term position to 30 November 2027 at Academic Level B.Parramatta City Campus.Salary: $125,177 – $147,810 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Shape future finance graduates thr Reference 11605e60-54ae-40be-a995-73258a97790b Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Manager, IT Service Management - Digital Services Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit Digital Services (U76B) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 9.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $139,747 – $149,238 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead enterprise IT servi Reference 77653bd1-243b-49da-bb96-0a480288384a Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Remuneration & Benefits Specialist Salary Location Richmond, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Richmond Business Unit People and Culture (U76E) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing position at HEW Level 8.Hawkesbury and Parramatta South campuses with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 p.a., plus 17% Super and Leave Loading. Lead remuner Reference 0ac8e10e-d401-4a3e-9b53-fc5fc92fbefe Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Placement Officer Salary Location Goulburn, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Goulburn Business Unit Faculty of Soc.Sciences,Art,Business,Education&Law (U73L) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, Ongoing position at HEW Level 6.Goulburn campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $99,159 – $106,284 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Coordinate student placements with Reference 310234af-aaad-4187-a68b-a86fa24531ef Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Director, Global Program Liaison Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Global Partnerships & Transnational Education (U73N) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Senior Description Full-time, Senior Position on a 5-Year Fixed-Term Contract.Parramatta South campus with flexible working arrangements.Competitive senior-level remuneration, commensurate with experience.Lead the gove Reference 6a621932-48ef-4fb5-b7ef-67af0297c0eb Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Senior Officer, Research Infrastructure Partnerships and Operations Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Faculty of Health (U73M) Contract Type Casual Position Category Professional Description Casual, short-term appointment at HEW Level 8, up to 35 hours per week.Campbelltown campus with work at Campbelltown Hospital as required.Casual hourly rate: $82.72 to $91.82, plus Superannuation.Lea Reference 2f8323cb-f421-49d9-8cf1-64bd8804104d Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Strategic Project Coordinator Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Operations Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Data (U76A) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, ongoing positionBased at Western’s Parramatta South campusSalary: HEW Level 7 $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave LoadingShape and implement strategies that strengthen d Reference e7b047f8-911b-4942-9fc6-3642219bbd0b Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Change Analyst, Cyber Salary Location Parramatta, AU Division Vice-Chancellor & President Brand Western Sydney University Location Parramatta Business Unit Strategy & Transformation (U47D) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full time, fixed term position until 12 August 2027Based at Western’s Parramatta South campus, with flexible working arrangementsSalary: HEW Level 7 $108,659 – $117,202 per annum, plus 17% Super and L Reference 8be7fd5c-8b3c-4b8c-8cc7-e5afa74ad1d4 Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Clinical Trials Manager Salary Location Campbelltown, AU Division Provost Brand Western Sydney University Location Campbelltown Business Unit Faculty of Health (U73M) Contract Type Full-Time Position Category Professional Description Full-time, 2 Years Fixed-Term position at HEW Level 8.Campbelltown campus with flexible working arrangements.Salary: $120,754 – $134,051 per annum, plus 17% Super and Leave Loading.Lead the Faculty’s Reference e79659b3-440d-431b-a92f-f1587fe778fc Expiry Date 01/01/0001 Read more Shortlist Read more Shortlist Apply"
